CORE no-new-smt
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ u >= 2\^53: SUCCESS$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Control for the SMT2 float-to-integer regression test (see test_smt2.desc): the
default SAT/boolbv back-end converts doubles in [2^53, 2^54) correctly, because
float_utilst::to_integer pre-pads the fraction before shifting.  This was the
reference behaviour the SMT2 back-end was fixed to match.
